entry.summary:
Your OpenAI call fails at 2am. Rate limit. Your script crashes, the entire pipeline stops, and the data you processed for the last hour is gone. If you're wrapping LLM calls in try/except with time.sleep(), you're doing it the hard way. Here's the fix in one decorator. import openai from tenacity import retry, stop_after_attempt, wait_exponential, retry_if_exception_type, before_sleep_log import logging
logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO) logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)
@retry( retry=retry_if_exception_type(( openai.RateLimitError, openai.APITimeoutError, openai.APIConnectionError, )), wait=wait_exponential(multiplier=1, min=2, max=30), stop=stop_after_attempt(3), before_sleep=before_sleep_log(logger, logging.WARNING), ) def call_llm(p…
